      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sepulcher of Order [zone=815]\n**Who:**\n- Alchemist Vaskerin [npc=39333]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Alaran Language:** | 88\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Alsa Thel Droplet [item=57563]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Infiltrator Tesara [npc=39339]\n- Therin the Ancient [npc=39335]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Dismantling the Order [quest=5710]\n- Sepulcher #2: Crafting the Triumvirate's Downfall [quest=5532]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Dec 13 22:01:35 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a solo task that starts with Alchemist Vaskerin in the Sepulcher of Order (located at about 460, 415, 12 -- from the main building's entrance room, head west until you come to Vaskerin)._\n_While it has no pre-requisites and isn't part of a series, it is a sub-task you have to complete in order to finish \"Crafting the Triumvirate's Downfall\" [quest=5532]._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- No tasks\n\\- 88 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, Alchemist Vaskerin'\nAlchemist Vaskerin says 'I did not think this tomb would be warm. Far before my memory, the sepulcher was sealed away, and it has been centuries since any living soul has entered. I thought we would be huddled around braziers, but the glowing [liquid] everywhere -- the alsa thel the thelasas call it -- still pours from the bodies of the Triumvirate and heats the cavern.'\nYou say, 'Liquid?'\nAlchemist Vaskerin says 'The Triumvirate must be stirring. If their blood lives, their bodies will soon follow. Their power will be absolute. I do not doubt this. I have seen firsthand the power of the alsa thel. Do you know of the [thel ereth ril] that wander these halls?'\nYou say, 'What about the thel ereth ril?'\nAlchemist Vaskerin says 'They contain the purified essence of the alsa thel, and they bestow great vitality upon the loyal servants of the Triumvirate. The thel ereth ril themselves do not know death: I saw an unruly goral slash at one's throat, but the thel ereth ril walked on as if nothing happened, the glowing wound upon its neck closing almost instantly. This made me question whether nothing could [kill it].'\nYou say, 'Kill it?'\nAlchemist Vaskerin says 'I surely will be reprimanded for this, but I do not care. Whenever the thel ereth ril come near, I feel an overwhelming sense of dread. I have done much research on the alsa thel, and I believe I have found a way to neutralize the vitality of the thel ereth ril. It is not easy, though. I need many samples of alsa thel that can be found suffused in the blood of creatures that inhabit this sepulcher. If you could [collect] the samples, I think it would be possible to test my theories on the thel ereth ril.'\nYou say, 'I'll collect some samples'\nAlchemist Vaskerin says 'I shall await your return. Then we will see if the thel ereth ril are truly immortal.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'To Kill a Thel Ereth Ril'.\nVaskerin has asked you to collect droplets of alsa thel from the creatures inside Sepulcher. With these droplets, Vaskerin can fashion a weapon that will cripple the thel ereth ril.\n\n---\n\nCollect 500 Alsa Thel Droplets 0/500 (ALL)\nSpeak with Alchemist Vaskerin 0/1 (Sepulcher of Order)\n_Alsa Thel Droplets are found via two methods:_\n_\\- As a reward from shared tasks given out by Infiltrator Tesara (9-14 droplets per shared task completed -- a full task list is found below this writeup)._\n_\\- It drops occasionally from mobs in each of the three Sepulcher zones (it will take you quite a long time to collect enough if doing it by drops alone)._\n_**NOTE:** The droplets are pre-lootable. Any droplets already in your inventory will automatically update the task._\n_Upon completion:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Alchemist Vaskerin'\nAlchemist Vaskerin says 'This is precisely what I need. Here, I have fused the droplets of alsa thel. Now, if you smith this hollow rod with the droplets, I believe we can strip the thel ereth ril of their power. Perhaps now I will be able to work here in peace! Go, do with this knowledge what you will. Just do not tell anyone where you received this information!'\nVaskerin has told you to combine the Aggregate Alsa Thel Droplet with Vaskerin's Hollow Rod in order to create a weapon that can cripple the thel ereth ril.\n_Final Reward:_\n900 platinum\nExperience (approximately 6 AAs at Level 95)\n_You also receive \"Vaskerin's Hollow Rod\" and \"Aggregate Alsa Thel Droplet\". Combine these in a forge to produce \"Rod of Alsa Thel\" for use in later Sepulcher tasks and missions._\n\n---\n\n**Tesara's Tasks**\n\\- Dismantling the Order [quest=5710]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Find Therin the Ancient (entrance of the building) and Alchemist Vaskerin (west from the building's entry room)._\n_NOTE: This task is solo and non-repeatable. All other tasks listed here are shared (1-6 players) and require that you've completed \"Dismantling the Order\"._\n_Say \"task\" to Infiltrator Tesara and you'll be offered one of 24 shared tasks (sorted here by the location in which they take place; links point to the individual task listing)._\n**Splendor**\n\\- Illegal Mining [quest=5711]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the far northwestern part of the zone (northwestern-most entrance to Sepulcher West) and use the \"Resplendent Mining Pick\" given to you to mine crystals in the rocks (3 updates). Note: You may encounter mob aggro as you do this._\n\\- Target the Healers [quest=5712]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the far northwestern part of the zone (northwestern-most entrance to Sepulcher West). Kill 4 crystalline healers._\n**Battle**\n\\- Taming the Living Blades [quest=5713]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the west side of the zone (the upper of the two middle entrances to Sepulcher West), beat living blades to low health, and use the \"Weapon Gravitator\" you received to gather their blades. Then with those weapons, kill 2 carnifexes, soldiers, or archons._\n\\- The Heat of Battle [quest=5714]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the west side of the zone (the upper of the two middle entrances to Sepulcher West) and kill 4 mobs affected with \"Heat of Battle\" (buffed on them near the front of the zone entrance)._\n**Tides**\n\\- Electrocution Danger [quest=5715]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _With the \"Water Spark\" received, travel to the west side of the zone (the lower of the two middle entrances to Sepulcher West) and use the spark to electrocute creatures there. They'll need to be killed after being shocked (4 mobs)._\n\\- High Tide [quest=5716]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the west side of the zone (the lower of the two middle entrances to Sepulcher West). As mobs wander the area, they'll pass through three different tidal clouds, each of which grants the mob a buff. Kill 3 mobs that have all three buffs on them._\n**Decay**\n\\- The Cloud of Decay [quest=5717]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the far southwestern part of the zone (southwestern-most entrance to Sepulcher West). Kill several mobs to create a Cloud of Decay, and then kill 4 mobs that get affected by this cloud._\n\\- Summation of Nightmares [quest=5718]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the far southwestern part of the zone (southwestern-most entrance to Sepulcher West). Weaken a skeleton and a soul creature at the same time to make them change into a revolting nightmare. Kill 2 revolving nightmares._\n**Fertility**\n\\- Trimming the Overgrowth [quest=5719]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the far southeastern part of the zone (southeastern-most entrance to Sepulcher East). Kill mobs there to make sprout piles spawn. Kill 15 sprout piles for the update._\n\\- Severing the Vines [quest=5720]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the far southeastern part of the zone (southeastern-most entrance to Sepulcher East). Kill 4 mobs with the \"Regeneration of Lunanyn\" buff on them._\n**Beasts**\n\\- Raptor Rampage [quest=5721]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the east side of the zone (the lower of the two middle entrances to Sepulcher East). Kill a goral, take its egg, and feed it to a raptor to cause it to go on a rampage. Do this 3 times._\n\\- Beastly Scavengers [quest=5722]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the east side of the zone (the lower of the two middle entrances to Sepulcher East). Pull mobs into the burrows and kill them there to lure a scavenging brute to the location. Kill 2 scavenging brutes._\n**Magic**\n\\- Confront Your Nemesis [quest=5723]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the east side of the zone (the upper of the two middle entrances to Sepulcher East). Fight mobs there to be transformed and then kill mobs while you're transformed. Kill 3 mobs while transformed._\n\\- Harmonious Magic [quest=5724]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the east side of the zone (the upper of the two middle entrances to Sepulcher East). Kill 4 denizens of magic while they are resonating with \"Harmonious Magic\". Pull creatures into the aura of their magic type to activate resonance_\n**Oratory**\n\\- Inherit the Wind [quest=5725]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the far northeastern part of the zone (northeastern-most entrance to Sepulcher East). Use the mystical auras present to reach the rocks and be enchanted by the spell. Kill 4 denizens of oratory (mobs outside the entrance)._\n\\- Condeming the Next Generation [quest=5726]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the far northeastern part of the zone (northeastern-most entrance to Sepulcher East). Kill the wind eggs spawned by the drakes._\n**The Triumvirate's Tomb**\n\\- Descend to Ascend [quest=5727]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the north-central part of the zone (the Triumvirate's territory where you'll find numerous blind dreamers around). Here, you'll find several alsa thel pools. Occasionally, initiates that wander the pools will be transformed by them. Kill a transformed initiate._\n\\- Become the Thel Ereth Ril [quest=5728]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _While under the illusion \"Form of the Thel Ereth Ril\", kill 4 followers of the Triumvirate (north-central part of the zone)._\n\\- Conquest of the Triumvirate [quest=5729]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the north-central part of the zone (the Triumvirate's territory where you'll find numerous blind dreamers around). Pull mobs out of the tomb area so that they lose their \"Conquest of the Triumvirate\" buff and kill them. Do this for 4 mobs._\n\\- Persuading the Weak Minded [quest=5730]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the north-central part of the zone (the Triumvirate's territory where you'll find numerous blind dreamers around). Weaken initiates and use the \"Commanding Words\" on them, then lead them in attacks against alsa constructs._\n**The Residences**\n\\- The Hunger of Thel [quest=5731]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Travel to the far north-central part of the zone (past the Triumvirate tomb area) and kill undead mobs (skeletons; zombies) that are buffed with \"Hunger of Thel\". Kill the ones in the areas with the fountains in the living quarters, or pull others into that area._\n\\- Secreting Supplies [quest=5732]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Steal boxes of supplies (found along the northernmost walls of Sepulcher) and deliver them to Tasara without being attacked._\n**Randoms**\n\\- Gift of Stabbing [quest=5733]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Daggers infused with alsa thel can be found scattered throughout Sepulcher. Deliver 6 thel daggers to Tasara._\n\\- Touched by a Thel Ereth Ril [quest=5734]\n\\-\\-\\-------- _Kill a creature empowered by the thel ereth ril (buffed with \"Aegis of Alsa Thel\")._\n- Aggregate Alsa Thel Droplet [item=50541]\n- Rod of Alsa Thel [item=57558]\n- Vaskerin's Hollow Rod [item=101683]",
